  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed for both automatic and manual lighting. Common in traffic contexts ({信号|しんごう}の{点灯|てんとう} — traffic light activation), event contexts (tree-lighting ceremonies), and everyday appliance descriptions.\n\nBe careful not to confuse with homophones: {店頭|てんとう} (storefront) and {転倒|てんとう} (falling over).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {点灯|てんとう}する (to light up, to turn on)\n- {点灯|てんとう}{式|しき} (lighting ceremony)\n- ランプが{点灯|てんとう}する (a lamp turns on)\n- {警告灯|けいこくとう}が{点灯|てんとう}する (a warning light comes on)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {消灯|しょうとう}: lights out — the opposite; turning off lights\n- {点|つ}ける: to turn on — casual, everyday equivalent",
